<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Trapezoidal rule from a table of offsets</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} measured [[if test="is(pl=0)"]]a plot beside a road near Nyeri[[elif test="is(pl=1)"]]a vegetable garden at a school in Kisii[[elif test="is(pl=2)"]]a maize field in Trans Nzoia[[elif test="is(pl=3)"]]a flower farm plot near Naivasha[[else]]a coffee shamba in Kiambu[[/if]]. Along a straight fence \({@Lf@}\,\text{m}\) long, starting at one corner, {@pr@} measured the distance (the offset) from the fence to the curved edge of the plot every \({@h@}\,\text{m}\).</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Distance along fence (m)</th>[[foreach u="xs"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@u@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Offset (m)</th>[[foreach u="ys"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr></table><p>(a) How many strips do these measurements make?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Use the trapezoidal rule to estimate the area of the plot.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) There are \({@n+1@}\) offsets. The strips are the gaps between them, so there are \({@n@}\) strips, each \(h = {@h@}\,\text{m}\) wide: \({@Lf@} \div {@h@} = {@n@}\).</p><p>(b) Each inner offset is a side of two trapezia, so it is counted twice. Multiply each offset by its weight:</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Offset (m)</th>[[foreach u="ys"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Weight</th>[[foreach u="wts"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@u@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Weight \(\times\) offset</th>[[foreach u="wys"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr></table><p>\[A \approx \tfrac{1}{2}h\left[y_0 + y_{ {@n@} } + 2(y_1 + \cdots + y_{ {@n-1@} })\right] = \tfrac{1}{2} \times {@h@} \times {@exd(first(ys)+last(ys)+2*inner)@} = {@exd(Ta)@}\,\text{m}^2\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: trapezoidal rule from a table of survey offsets: count the strips from the ordinates, then apply the rule. Entries [place, h, offsets]. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 9, Example 8. */
L: [[0,10,[24,31,35,33,28]],[1,5,[12,15,17,18,16,13]],[2,20,[45,52,58,55,49,40,34]],[3,10,[18,22,27,29,26]],[4,4,[9,11,14,15,13,10]],[0,5,[20,24,26,25,21,18,15]],[1,20,[60,66,70,68,61]],[2,10,[15,21,24,22,23,19]],[3,4,[15/2,9,21/2,11,19/2,8,13/2]],[4,10,[33,36,40,37,30]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
pl: L[ix][1]; h: L[ix][2]; ys: L[ix][3];
n: length(ys)-1;
Lf: n*h;
inner: apply("+",rest(rest(ys),-1));
Ta: h/2*(first(ys)+last(ys)+2*inner);
xs: makelist(j*h,j,0,n);
wts: makelist(if j=0 or j=n then 1 else 2,j,0,n);
wys: makelist(wts[j]*ys[j],j,1,n+1);
NP: rand([["Atieno","she"],["Mutua","he"],["Chebet","she"],["Ouma","he"]]);
nm: NP[1]; pr: NP[2];
/* diagnostics */
T2: 2*Ta;
Thalf: h/2*apply("+",ys);
Th: h*apply("+",ys);
Tends: h/2*(2*(first(ys)+last(ys))+inner);
Tw: (Lf/(n+1))/2*(first(ys)+last(ys)+2*inner);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
